          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ठिगणो (ṭhigṇo) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from ṭhiṅga, \"defective\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants. CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry (CDIAL 5501); the match is through Hindi ṭhĩgnā and Gujarati ṭhĩgṇũ. CDIAL sets it in a large group of \"defective\" words; Hindi and Gujarati forms mean \"dwarfish\"."
